  "preamble": "Deaffrication of the voiceless dental affricate [ts] to the interdental fricative [θ], with the stop phase lost and the fricative fronted to a non-sibilant. In Albanian, the Proto-Albanian affricate *ts (mostly from PIE *ḱ) became th [θ] (*tsurja > thur 'to plait'), and Thao and Old Persian show the same outcome. In Castilian Spanish, Galician and some Venetan dialects the old affricate also ended up as [θ], but through an attested intermediate dental sibilant [s̪].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deaffrication, Interdentalization, Loss of Sibilance",
  "languageExamples": [
